At 320x568, idle scrollH 794 vs win 568 — page scrolls, which is acceptable but the game is below the fold initially. The hero scrolls; the arena-footer with START may be below the fold on very short phones. The user can scroll. But during play, footerBottom 576 > 568 by 8px, scrollH 589. Slight scroll. It's a very small screen; acceptable but could compact more at max-height 650. Existing media `max-height:800` reduces. Add a stronger `max-height:640` query: hide intro paragraph? On idle, scroll is expected for a 568px screen; but the key START button should ideally be visible.

Let me check idle element positions at 320x568: hero probably 794 tall, footer at bottom off-screen. That's a usability issue: pressing start requires scrolling. Prior version likely similar. Add for max-height 640: hide `.intro p` and shrink h1, tighten stage, pads. Let's compute idle heights: topbar 40 + intro (~28+50+13+? ~200) + players ~68 + stage 230 + footer 100 (mobile grid) + padding 20 = ~660. Still > 568. To fit, hide intro entirely on short screens? Then ~460. Simpler: at max-height 640, apply `.intro{display:none}` always (even idle) and show brand/topbar. But then first-time users miss instructions; they have HOW TO PLAY. Acceptable on tiny landscape screens.

Alternatively let the page scroll; games are often below the fold on small phones. But the START button being off-screen on initial load is bad. A compromise: `@media(max-height:640px){.intro p{display:none}.intro h1{font-size:40px;margin:6px 0}.intro{padding:14px}...}`. Estimate: topbar 40 + intro (56+40+12) ≈ 110 + players 66 + stage 190 + footer 100 = 506 + padding 20 = 526 < 568. Good. Add this media query.

